WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm definitely gonna be the first-star idol!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.520
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:18.280
With that said, on the next It's Our Job To Shine, 
we'll be doing a special program! {jikai. this was my fault}

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.580
S4's...

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.580
"We'll Have Shining Career Experiences!"{shouldn't this be in sentence form like the other things?}{sure}

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:29.590
We'll be taking on all sorts of one-day careers, like being a police chief or a pâtissière.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:35.090
This project will put the four of us in S4 through a variety of jobs.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:40.720
But the thing is, not even <i>we</i> have any idea what's awaiting us!

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:47.060
Just like all you viewers out there, all of us are anticipexcited for it! {these are the only two times it appears in the episode and I want some sort of noticable word}

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.000
I saw your program.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.510
What one-day careers could be in store?

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:40.340
We could be the manager of a beach hut or a pool lifeguard!

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.260
It sounds as though you have summer on your mind.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.890
That's 'cause summer's right after the rainy season!

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:51.400
I've loved summer ever since I was a kid!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.610
You certainly have.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.280
That affects you too, Lilienne.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.410
Don't you need to spend this year at the plateau like you always do?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:07.660
I love summer, but whenever I don't get to spend time with you...

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.290
It's no fun.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.960
No, I plan to spend this summer at Four Star Academy.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.840
But...

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:25.600
Now that I have been granted a Star Premium Rare Coord, I feel as though I can overcome any obstacle in my path.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:27.720
Lilienne...

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.100
As proof of that...

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.810
I have decided to participate in a certain event.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.110
Harasho!

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:42.160
Gothic Victoria would like to express its gratitude for everyone's support.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.580
Therefore we will be holding a fan appreciation tour for a few lucky lottery winners.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.250
The destination will be the Suzukaze Plateau.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:52.000
<b>\h\h\h\hSuzukaze Plateau\h\h\h\h</b>

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:52.000
<b>\h\h\h\hSuzukaze Plateau\h\h\h\h</b>

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:54.630
And if you can believe it, the tour guide will be... Shirogane Lily! {I checked, we didn't do anything special for his -deshou}{how convenient}

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.920
Huh? You're gonna be a tour guide?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.090
Yes.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:05.390
A stage will also be built for me at the Suzukaze Plateau.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:10.730
The Suzukaze Plateau... isn't that where you retreat to every summer?

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.060
Yes.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:19.320
And around the area are a number of locations famous for their beauty.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:29.830
When I first received the offer, I considered 
declining as I thought I would be incapable.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.870
However, were I able to complete this event...

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.920
I would be able to spend the summer with you.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.300
Will you support me, Yuzu?

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.180
I know for sure that you'll be able to make it through, Lilienne.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.020
Yes.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:54.690
This plan gets me going!

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.190
I just need to join!

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.780
It's a good chance to repay Lily-senpai for all she's done.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.690
Yeah!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.820
Now that I have accepted, I must do the necessary preparations.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.450
I see.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:17.500
That majestic lake on the way to the plateau used to be a volcanic crater.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.710
And also,

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:23.590
the valley with a constant refreshing breeze was actually carved out by a glacier.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:30.510
There were even dinosaur fossils discovered in the rock formations nearby.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:35.390
Ouroscopyosaurus... what could it have been like? {totally made up}{sure}

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.810
A sauropod striding across the land...

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.530
Perhaps it was a fearsome carnivore!

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.910
Let's welcome today's tour's special guide!

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.080
And here she is!

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:06.300
I am your tour guide Shirogane Lily, and I will do my utmost to make this a pleasant and enjoyable experience.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.800
Let us set off for the Suzukaze Plateau.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.260
Okay!

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.890
Ouch! We're missing a guest! What now?

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:20.560
The next train won't make it for the concert.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.730
Excuse me.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:27.700
We can't push back the concert any further, or the tour schedule will suffer.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:32.700
All participants were told about the strict timetable. We have no choice.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.040
Although I do feel bad...

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.750
Please wait!

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:40.880
That person must have been looking forward to this tour very much.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.840
Can we really do nothing for them?

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.170
Lily-senpai?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.010
Ako?

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.130
What are you doing here?

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.140
What about you? And what's with the outfit?

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:55.470
I have been appointed as the one-day station master for our program.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.520
One-day station manager?

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:02.020
Please be mindful of safety and refrain from pushing onto a train.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.070
That does sound like a problem.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.780
I wish to wait for them if possible.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.200
But the direct train to the plateau is departing soon.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.530
They're here!

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.330
I was so excited I could hardly sleep, 
and ended up not waking up in time.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.620
I'm so sorry!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.460
Hold on!

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:28.260
Why couldn't you wait just a moment more?

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:32.430
Our railway company's motto is "on time, all the time".

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.850
At this point, we can only cancel the tour.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.230
Everyone was so very excited for it...

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.940
Tick tick tick tick...

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.360
Ding-dong!

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:51.780
According to my mental database, 
you can take the next local train for five stops.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:56.990
Then switch lines and take the express to the eighth stop...

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.120
And you'll get ahead of the direct line! {I don't think that would work}{maybe if their motto were "on time, some of the time, all of the time"}

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.500
You have the entire schedule memorized?

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.330
S4 is incredible...

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:08.500
You should expect nothing less from a one-day station master.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.840
Could you please reserve seats for their groups on each of the trains,

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.640
<i>every</i>-day station master?

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.180
Yes, of course.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.760
I am in your debt.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.770
Harasho!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.350
You want to follow them and continue shooting?

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.360
True, this should provide for a rather interesting show.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:37.620
Attention, everyone. We will momentarily begin the scheduled lunch time.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.660
We forgot the station bento? {damn, I never named these in episode 24 OG}

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.010
We forgot the station bento?

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:04.190
The staff forgot to load it in the chaos of trying to change trains.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:08.020
There's not much we can do. 
I'll explain the circumstances to—

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:09.520
Please wait!

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:12.780
Eating station bento on a train is an irreplaceable experience.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.280
Isn't there anything we can do?

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:20.370
Would anyone like hot coffee, or perhaps a cold beverage?

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.580
Mahiru-san!

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.000
Lily-senpai?

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:30.040
I see. So your one-day career was as a train attendant. {technically a sales cart person}

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:34.170
That's perfect! You should have a whole bunch of lunches then, right?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.260
Huh?

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.430
Well, actually...

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:42.140
Mahiru-chan from S4 is the bento lady!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:45.140
Three fluffy-drippy veggie omelette rice bento, please!

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:49.400
I'll take ten thick and rich demi-glace hamburg sets!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.940
Ah, okay! Right away!

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:56.570
So all I've got left now are drinks.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:57.780
I'm sorry.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:01.370
Please, you are not at fault.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.450
However...

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.590
Is it possible to prepare any more?

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.470
Mahiru-chan!

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.850
They said that there are still some left over.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.560
Really?

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.900
Thanks for the food!

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:46.000
Due to problems with the overhead wiring, this train is unable to continue operation.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.120
What?

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:02.890
With the train stuck here, I can't imagine Lily-senpai's tour happening.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:08.980
L-Look up there!

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.650
Lilienne!

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.650
Lilienne!

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.910
Yuzu?!

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:24.330
Here I come!

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:31.170
I gotcha.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:36.670
You were in such a pinch that I felt a tingling thirty thousand feet high.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:42.430
But not even you can get a train moving without electricity.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:46.430
There's more than one way to get to the plateau.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:59.030
Five or ten helicopters is an easy enough request to fill for our one-day chief purser. {https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purser#Aircraft}

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:03.070
We'll be at the plateau in no time! Go, go, go!

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.410
Now there's a sudden storm?!

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.500
Yuzu, the weather report!

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:12.870
Roger!

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:21.010
Next up is your one-day weathercaster, Nijino Yume, with the weather forecast for the Suzukaze Plateau.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.420
Yume-san!

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:26.180
The area is currently wracked with severe storms,

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:30.180
but they should clear up without a trace in no time.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:35.190
A storm like this won't so easily go away. We should turn back.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:39.440
But that would make this the end of Lily-senpai's tour!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.190
Chief purser.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.280
Lilienne.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.450
I will believe in Yume-san!

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:51.950
Roger!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.840
We're clear of the storm!

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.840
Something is strange!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.300
We should be directly above the Suzukaze Plateau,

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:10.220
so why don't I see the stage lights anywhere?

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:12.850
This is trouble!

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:16.600
The entire surrounding area has been hit by a blackout!

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.230
That must be why the train stopped.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:24.570
Even if we make it down, we'll have no way of illuminating the stage.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.990
All is lost...

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.030
Lily-senpai!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.990
Lilienne!

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:37.000
I just wanted to make it through this tour... and spend the summer together...

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.000
Lilienne!

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.990
Ouroscopyosaurus?!

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.300
Lilienne.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.470
Yuzu!

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:28.760
Yume!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.720
You okay, Rola?

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.720
You two, it is about time.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.730
Everyone...

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.230
It was all this Ouroscopyosaurus's fault.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:44.230
The reason that fan was late, 
the reason they forgot the lunches,

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:47.570
and the reason the train and stage lights lost power.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.610
But there's no need to worry.

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.280
We'll release our true power... {these two lines make no sense grammatically as far as I can tell}{looks like some semantic drift with チャレンジ which can mean a bunch of different things now}

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.250
As the Justice Heroine Rangers! {man I don't know}

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:32.070
He's tough.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.200
Let me handle it!

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.700
Saint Honoré!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:45.000
Crème Renversée à la Mode!

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:48.130
Dark Choco Brownie!

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.180
Tarte Méli-mélo!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:01.690
Well? What do you think of my Dad's confections?

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:06.730
As expected of Yume...'s Dad's sweets!

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.190
Yume-san!

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:11.450
Now then, would you fix the blackout?

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.490
Ouroscopyosaurus?

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:27.170
Now I will be able to see my concert through...

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.590
Lily-senpai!

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:31.220
Lilienne!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.260
I'm so glad...

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.600
Lilienne.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.430
Lilienne!

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.110
Yuzu...

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:48.860
Lilienne!

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:52.320
What about the Ouroscopyosaurus?

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.360
Huh?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.240
And the blackout?

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.870
So it was a dream.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:05.620
A dream?

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:13.010
I was up rather late last night preparing to be a tour guide.

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:18.600
Then the stage must still be...

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:30.020
Now that I look around, why is it so bright even though we're in a blackout?

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.290
We made a radio announcement.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:54.460
All of S4's and Rola's and your fans gathered here for you.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:58.930
This many of them?

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.810
Isn't it bright?

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.850
Yes.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.810
And their light feels so warm.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:10.310
Can you sing, Lilienne?

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.360
Of course.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:18.450
This is the one way I could possibly repay them.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:26.120
For everyone who gave me this opportunity to express my gratitude.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.960
Shirogane Lily, pouring my soul into this moment!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:55.980
I vow eternal radiance upon this dress!

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.700
Harasho!

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:58.000
The Pluto-winged Star Premium Rare Coord.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:01.670
It's marvelous every time I see it.

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:07.220
It conveys how extraordinary Gothic Victoria is to such a large audience.

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:09.970
She's amazing.

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:15.850
Even after getting her Star Wings, not only has she kept moving, but she's even sped up further.

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:16.730
Yeah.

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:20.940
This summer's Tundra Diva...

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:23.190
...is gonna be hot!

00:23:55.870 --> 00:24:01.330
The Tundra Diva is shining even brighter in her Pluto Star Premium Rare Coord.

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:05.960
I need to learn from Lily-senpai, with how she strives for even greater heights even after she got her Star Wings.

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:10.010
Yeah! I definitely want Star Wings of my own too.

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:13.590
I devote myself to Elza!

00:24:13.590 --> 00:24:15.100
She's like a real prince.

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:18.100
But doesn't she care about her own Aikatsu?

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:20.060
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:21.560
Wish upon a star.

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:23.900
Become the first-star idol!
